{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide","id":198652,"title":"Demon Translation Guide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-16T00:44:36-07:00","id":198652,"title":"Demon Translation Guide","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I've noticed of late that the Monday Morning blog has been talking about the Translation Guide being in development/writing/etc. now.<br /> <br /> It's the book I am most looking forward to seeing, are there any hints of the direction your taking or general ethos or big design decisions you've already made you can share?<br /> <br /> Will you be trying to merge Lores into something that uses Embeds/Exploits or rewriting the Lores to work better in an nWoD environment? Will you be doing a direct 'literal' translation of some of the powers available or will you be doing some of the (much needed!) errataing and tweaking that the creaky old D:tF needed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T01:38:11-07:00","id":198700,"title":"","content":"I'd say that it's best not to get your hopes up, but then I'd be a hypocrite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T01:45:11-07:00","id":198709,"title":"","content":"Rose has already answered one aspect of your question \u2014 Lores aren't being converted into Embeds or Exploits, but are being translated as distinct power trees of their own. I'm interested to see how it turns out too, although the translation guides have been kind of a letdown for me each time so far. But there's always a first time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T04:53:50-07:00","id":198809,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t hold my breath for the DTG being an update to DtF; it\u2019s most likely to limit itself to translating DtD material into terms compatible with DtF and vice versa. It <i>is</i>, after all, a <i>Translation</i> Guide. That said, porting elements of DtF into nWoD has some interesting possibilities: if the God-Machine is, in effect, the Demiurge of Gnosticism, then the God of DtF could be adapted for use as Gnosticism\u2019s Creator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:16:53-07:00","id":199022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=198709#post198709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rose has already answered one aspect of your question \u2014 Lores aren't being converted into Embeds or Exploits, but are being translated as distinct power trees of their own. I'm interested to see how it turns out too, although the translation guides have been kind of a letdown for me each time so far. But there's always a first time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alongside That, Torment isn't a power or morality stat, but a third unique stat that you can use right alongside Cover and Primum.<br /> <br /> I am all teh excites for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:11:23-07:00","id":199093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=199022#post199022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alongside That, Torment isn't a power or morality stat, but a third unique stat that you can use right alongside Cover and Primum.<br /> <br /> I am all teh excites for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh?<br /> <br /> So you could merge Cover with a D:tF style Demon?<br /> <br /> I appreciate some of the concepts of D:tD in an intellectual sense and would happily merge them into a D:tF aesthetic game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:24:58-07:00","id":199097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=199022#post199022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am all teh excites for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would hope not to feel that same way on account of fear of disappointment, but I kind of DO feel the same way. The BIGGEST reason for that feeling is because of how much I learned about <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b> (a game I'd played for decades) by reading the <i>Vampire Translation Guide</i>'s treatment of Clans, Disciplines, etc. in light of them appearing in <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b>. Same goes for <i>Mage Translation Guide</i>. I know the 'classic' <b>Demon</b> game as well as I know <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, and I'm sure that the <b>Demon</b> book shall only serve to increase how much I know...<br /> <br /> Actually, more to the point, the translation books have given me ideas about how either the classic or current World of Darkness games they covered can be enhanced, made more mysterious, chopped and rebuilt. I look forward to seeing how both version of <b>Demon</b> can EVEN be made scarier!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T14:22:09-07:00","id":199261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=199097#post199097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would hope not to feel that same way on account of fear of disappointment, but I kind of DO feel the same way. The BIGGEST reason for that feeling is because of how much I learned about <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b> (a game I'd played for decades) by reading the <i>Vampire Translation Guide</i>'s treatment of Clans, Disciplines, etc. in light of them appearing in <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b>. Same goes for <i>Mage Translation Guide</i>. I know the 'classic' <b>Demon</b> game as well as I know <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, and I'm sure that the <b>Demon</b> book shall only serve to increase how much I know...<br /> <br /> Actually, more to the point, the translation books have given me ideas about how either the classic or current World of Darkness games they covered can be enhanced, made more mysterious, chopped and rebuilt. I look forward to seeing how both version of <b>Demon</b> can EVEN be made scarier!</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the coolest things about the Translation Guide series is how it focuses the core concepts the game lines. I &quot;get&quot; <b>Ascension </b>a lot more clearly because of the Mage Translation Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T14:15:37-07:00","id":202365,"title":"","content":"One thing that would interest me there would be if the august date is doable or not.<br /> <br /> Aside from that from the things mentioned so far it sounds way more smooth than the other translationguides to use (and that with the 2 demon rules having WAY less to do with each other than vampires rules or mages rules)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T17:35:14-07:00","id":202505,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m curious as to whether the <b>Demon Translation Guide</b> will say anything about <b>Inferno</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T23:21:38-07:00","id":202682,"title":"","content":"why should it? the translation guide is only about converting demons from owod to nwod and vice versa. at max the storyteller guide or something else could be mentioning inferno from what I see (but even that is questionable as a possible conneciton was mentioned in the core but inferno is still a completely different book)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T07:08:25-07:00","id":202877,"title":"","content":"Why should it? Because there are elements of <b>Inferno</b> that dovetail quite nicely with <b>Demon: the Fallen</b>. In particular, the Possessed from that book are close matches for the Fallen, and might be better recepticles for ports of <b>Fallen</b>\u2019s Lores, Houses, etc. than the Unchained are. There <i>might</i> even be some stuff from <b>Inferno</b> that could be ported into <b>Demon: the Fallen</b>.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T07:30:40-07:00","id":202888,"title":"","content":"I'm actually looking forward to the translation guide, so I can finally try out this idea I've had. Basically, I want to try converting the Great Houses from d20's Infernum into a game of infernal politics, one where the threat of Angels is constantly hanging like a sword of Damocles as the archfiends try to gain sovereignty over their fellow demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T13:39:13-07:00","id":203211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=202888#post202888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually looking forward to the translation guide, so I can finally try out this idea I've had. Basically, I want to try converting the Great Houses from d20's Infernum into a game of infernal politics, one where the threat of Angels is constantly hanging like a sword of Damocles as the archfiends try to gain sovereignty over their fellow demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have one player in my game waiting for it sitting on needles. We are using the idea that the angels and demons were originally like those in owod......then when the error was seen that angels are fallable the GM was created (or maybe it IS god even that was never fully decided) and mechanical insteadof &quot;biological&quot; angels were created as machines are not as fallible as biological things (possibly a few angelic cousins of the malefactors and devils doing this). but still need rules there or at least enough info to see if the idea can work with the translation guide or not^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T13:14:31-07:00","id":215009,"title":"","content":"Hmmm question is if it is still in the making or not. 2 Monday posts without a mention of the translation guide. And the status update of rose also didn't mention the translation guide at all. ( <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/demon-the-descent-updates/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/demon-the-descent-updates/</a> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T15:17:19-07:00","id":216192,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I can't wait for the Translation Guide... I'm writing my own fusion of Fallen and Descent in the mean time, because I'm getting impatient. xD (I know the writing team's got a lot on their hands, so I don't mind. It's a good mental exercise)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T15:21:17-07:00","id":216199,"title":"","content":"We're still doing it. But I haven't had time to work on it in a while, because of developing other supplements, like <i>The Demon Seed Collection</i> and the <i>Demon Storyteller's Guide</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T15:25:31-07:00","id":216206,"title":"","content":"I actually did something similar, Dreaminggod. Take a look: <a href=\"http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=4988.0\" target=\"_blank\">http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=4988.0</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T12:54:36-07:00","id":219371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=216199#post216199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're still doing it. But I haven't had time to work on it in a while, because of developing other supplements, like <i>The Demon Seed Collection</i> and the <i>Demon Storyteller's Guide</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any time estimate there already as to which month could be realistical? (I take it that august like in the current projects part is not really realistical there).<br /> <br /> On another note: Will the owod -&gt; nwod demons have the same energy stat as normal nwod demons or more something akin to faith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T18:48:31-07:00","id":219726,"title":"","content":"If previous Translation Guides are any indication, they\u2019re not going to port the Fallen into the nWoD in one big chunk: they\u2019ll break the Fallen up into component parts and will show how each part could be translated into the nWoD. Do you want Unchained who are powered by Faith instead of Primium? Do you want Unchained who use Lores instead of Embeds and Exploits? Do you want Unchained who contend with Torment rather than maintaining Cover? Do you want Unchained who Come from seven Houses rather than four Incarnations? Do you want an Agenda for the Unchained that resembles the Luciferans? Do you want the Unchained to be fighting the Demiurge (i.e., the God-Machine), completely changing the tone of their struggle<sup>*</sup>? Each of these, I suspect, will be independently available; and if you want to reassemble all of the pieces into nWoD Fallen, you should be free to do so. More generally, you should have the option to make the Unchained exactly as much like the Fallen as you want. That\u2019s what I\u2019m anticipating, at least.<hr />* The tones are so different that the one Agenda I have no interest in playing in <b>Descent</b> (the Integrators) corresponds directly to the one Faction that I\u2019m willing to play in <b>Fallen</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T00:21:24-07:00","id":219941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=219726#post219726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*The tones are so different that the one Agenda I have no interest in playing in <b>Descent</b> (the Integrators) corresponds directly to the one Faction that I\u2019m willing to play in <b>Fallen</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly I know of an apocryphal tale of a bible study group in my home town that met up in the back of a church on weekends who played Demon the Fallen with all of them being Reconcilers. They were essentially playing with the 'God has unlimited forgiveness' as the driving force, they just had to go out and <i>earn</i> it by being what amounted to Christian misionary crusader, charitable heroes. My understanding is that one of them found the book in their child's room and brought it along asking for advice on what to do about it!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T05:48:47-07:00","id":220079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=219371#post219371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any time estimate there already as to which month could be realistical? (I take it that august like in the current projects part is not really realistical there).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. And I'll tell ya why: Rose has a bunch of things she's writing/developing. I have a bunch, too (I have *three* core book-sized things I'm developing in 2014/2015, and the bulk of the work is before Xmas). When she gets a draft of the DTG done, I'll redline it as soon as I'm able, and going on past experience it'll be a pretty quick process at that point...but if I'm ass-deep in [OPP PROJECT 1] or [OPP PROJECT 2] or <b>Chill</b>, then it might take me a while to get to it. <br /> <br /> So the basic answer is: It'll be out just as soon as we can get it out, without sacrificing quality or sanity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T05:59:05-07:00","id":220082,"title":"","content":"I'd rather have a good book than have a lesser one quicker.<br /> <br /> Besides, I know you and Rose will make it suitably awesome. It's slightly annoying to not know (budgets)but it is not a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":