iv class=\"message\">According to the newsletter, the pdf should be up by Wednesday (at least for backers) on drivethru.</div> </div> </div> </div>question is though wednesday evening america time or during the day (evening would be 4 am my time^^')","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:00:16-07:00","id":566626,"title":"","content":"Usually earlier in the day for Americans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:08:27-07:00","id":566633,"title":"","content":"Then I'm hopeful I can read through it before I head to bed today <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T12:48:59-07:00","id":566819,"title":"","content":"Looking forward to this immensely!... though sadly, I got introduced to Demon too late to be an actual backer. If any kind soul would give us details from the advance PDF, I'd be super grateful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T12:49:55-07:00","id":566821,"title":"","content":"And Out! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/151502/Demon-Translation-Guide?src=newest_since\" target=\"_blank\">Grab the Demon Translation Guide Here!</a><br /> <br /> EDIT: only $5, and I can't afford it. Man, lean times suck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T13:02:29-07:00","id":566830,"title":"","content":"interesting<br /> Looked the whole time with the search<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?keywords=translation%20guide&amp;page=1&amp;sort=4a\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/themes/dtrpg/site-logo-redesignd.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?keywords=translation%20guide&amp;page=1&amp;sort=4a\" target=\"_blank\"> DriveThruRPG.com - The Largest RPG Download Store! </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?keywords=translation%20guide&amp;page=1&amp;sort=4a\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?keywords=translation%20guide&amp;page=1&amp;sort=4a </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Your one-stop online shop for new and vintage RPG products from the top publishers, delivered fresh to your desktop in electronic format. </div> </div> </div> <br /> and got nothing there^^' cool!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T13:07:04-07:00","id":566834,"title":"","content":"Argblarglgbglgbglgbglbglbglgbrlbglbglrblgl<br /> <br /> Bought it.<br /> <br /> Reading it.<br /> <br /> Radio silence until I am done. First D:tF product in ages!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T13:12:39-07:00","id":566837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=566834#post566834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Argblarglgbglgbglgbglbglbglgbrlbglbglrblgl<br /> <br /> Bought it.<br /> <br /> Reading it.<br /> <br /> Radio silence until I am done. First D:tF product in ages!</div> </div> </div> </div>*laughs at realizing how right you are*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T13:37:47-07:00","id":566882,"title":"","content":"Picked it up, did a quick readthrough. Some bullet points, starting with an overall first impression:<br /> <br /> <b>Verdict:</b> I like it better than any of the other translation guides to date, but I think the translation guides have been rather weak and this product isn't excluded. I don't really blame Eric so much as the very short wordcount in which he was asked to do so much; it's clear he worked to cram a lot of mechanical concepts in very short space.<br /> <br /> <b>Graphic layout:</b> Kinda ugly. Lots of clashing colors, specifically the illustrations. It would look better if the illustrations were consistently two-tone purple. I did like the bold contrast of the bright fire on the cover design, though.<br /> <br /> <b>It didn't have the one thing I was looking for most:</b> Quick nWoD rules for demons dropping the body and searching quickly for a new suitable host, vulnerable and ephemeral in the meantime. Since chat about the translation guide brought up concepts from Fallen that could be interesting in Descent, one of my group's players is looking towards a variant demon who lacks easy Cover-switching but seals more completely with a human &quot;host.&quot; We'll be able to homebrew it either way but it seemed like it could have saved us some time.<br /> <br /> <b>But it did have a lot of stuff:</b> The biggest letdown in the Werewolf Translation Guide was the way it attempted to convert the effects of Gifts through a universal mechanical filter rather than pay attention to individual powers. The Demon Translation Guide goes out of its way to avoid that. Lores, demonic form powers (from both Fallen and Descent), and even Merits and Backgrounds (again from both) are run down one by one, and many of them have brief mechanical implementations to use in the opposite game. The mechanical rigor isn't the most exact, but it's difficult to make that fit in so little space. Eric made a pretty game attempt.<br /> <br /> <b>That stuff also includes Sebettu Conditions:</b> So if you're brewing up alternative Agendas you can sub these in.<br /> <br /> <b>The best part was easily Hybrid Stories:</b> The final chapter provides something the past guides haven't: several setting alternatives for a cosmology that allows for the Fallen and the Unchained to coexist in a single world as two distinct types of fallen angel. There are some good ideas here, and the prose helps to break up the constant referring between books. A small majority of them lean towards folding the God-Machine into the Fallen cosmology as a sort of sub-phenomenon or deviation, but they generally do so pretty well, without damaging either perspective as characters. Another option has a simple but elegant solution that uses the fallen to represent an occasional byproduct of possession by demons from the Inferno. I would very much like to see a chapter like this in any future translation guides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T13:39:41-07:00","id":566883,"title":"","content":"Hm. Skimmed through a lot, and read most of it. I'll give it a more thorough pass soon. My wife will be glad this is out, she loves the Fallen. Only problem I noted is the lack of... well, Lore of Flames. It looks like it didn't get added after the page break.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T13:43:00-07:00","id":566888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=566883#post566883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Skimmed through a lot, and read most of it. I'll give it a more thorough pass soon. My wife will be glad this is out, she loves the Fallen. Only problem I noted is the lack of... well, Lore of Flames. It looks like it didn't get added after the page break.</div> </div> </div> </div>That looks intentional. Not all of the Lores receive an individual treatment for each level; there's a note that evocations unlisted should work as written, with the little table of difficulty tweaking. So the Lore of Flames only needed one evocation altered beyond simple dice mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T13:47:49-07:00","id":566892,"title":"","content":"Was kinda hoping for an actual, quick-ref translation for Descent's techno-terms into the more archaic flavoring of Fallen. You know, embed and exploits being called something more mystical, etc. Or at least having the option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T14:12:08-07:00","id":566931,"title":"","content":"One thing I missed (if I didn't ovelrook it that is): Earthbound. They are only mentioned in the fluff part a few times but nothing on how to best translate them or their powers (they have unique lores).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T14:28:26-07:00","id":567012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=566892#post566892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was kinda hoping for an actual, quick-ref translation for Descent's techno-terms into the more archaic flavoring of Fallen. You know, embed and exploits being called something more mystical, etc. Or at least having the option.</div> </div> </div> </div>It took me A Fucking Year to get around to it, but I made one for you, at least. You should see it bumped in the thread list, but it's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/205376-homebrew-demon-translation-lexicon?p=566985#post566985\">here</a>. Two versions, really! One specifically for the celestial aesthetics of a game of Fallen, and one for the plain language of Descent in ancient eras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T15:22:36-07:00","id":567061,"title":"","content":"Well for some of the systems not translated over (Being without a Host, possessing, Earthbound, ect) I have some of it translated for an upcoming game. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hwL5JQSynlW2k0ygXyQ5Of_iGztEpTGPmN9L2cAdFsk/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...L2cAdFsk/edit#</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T15:38:56-07:00","id":567072,"title":"","content":"I'm concerned about it being a bit late but feel like it's a sufficiently minor change, but could the word <b>schizophrenic </b>in reference to the God-Machine on pg 59 be changed to a another word? Mercurial or something else? I don't want to ruin anyone's fun but that's one of those words that feels very ugly when it's used in the literary sense, since schizophrenia is more complicated than simple inconsistent behavior, and the comparison is one of those unfortunate (and oftentimes unintentional) forms of ableism. It's just one of those small, socially conscious things that would be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T16:42:57-07:00","id":567122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=567072#post567072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm concerned about it being a bit late but feel like it's a sufficiently minor change, but could the word <b>schizophrenic </b>in reference to the God-Machine on pg 59 be changed to a another word? Mercurial or something else? I don't want to ruin anyone's fun but that's one of those words that feels very ugly when it's used in the literary sense, since schizophrenia is more complicated than simple inconsistent behavior, and the comparison is one of those unfortunate (and oftentimes unintentional) forms of ableism. It's just one of those small, socially conscious things that would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you're coming from, but I honestly don't know how else to describe its logic-known-only-to-itself.<br /> <br /> &quot;Chaotic&quot;, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T16:50:52-07:00","id":567128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=567122#post567122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see where you're coming from, but I honestly don't know how else to describe its logic-known-only-to-itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also the word came from attempting to describe the disconnect between perception, memory, personality and behavior that typifies the disorder, which is both where the general use takes its cues from and a fair match for the massive decentralized conspiracy-engine that occasionally causes Falls by giving mutually contradictory assignments to angels dispatched to the same area and can receive faulty data by virtue of both deliberate and unintentional sabotage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T18:18:09-07:00","id":567207,"title":"","content":"Were Analysts intentionally not included in the guide? Because I could understand why, but it'd be nice to have an existing mechanical conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T23:15:13-07:00","id":567459,"title":"","content":"I'm personally rather partial to the \u201cReformed Possessors\u201d setting option, which fits the Fallen into the nWoD by declaring them to be a variant of the Infernals \u2014 or, more specifically, a supercharged variant of the Possessed. You don't even need to involve the God-Machine or the Unchained in such a setting if you don't want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-25-2015, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T04:41:23-07:00","id":567641,"title":"","content":"Mightily pleased, lots to work with here, guidance on what to do and some nice ideas for integrating both. Excited to port this into my games <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T04:45:50-07:00","id":567647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=566882#post566882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The best part was easily Hybrid Stories:</b> The final chapter provides something the past guides haven't: several setting alternatives for a cosmology that allows for the Fallen and the Unchained to coexist in a single world as two distinct types of fallen angel. There are some good ideas here, and the prose helps to break up the constant referring between books. A small majority of them lean towards folding the God-Machine into the Fallen cosmology as a sort of sub-phenomenon or deviation, but they generally do so pretty well, without damaging either perspective as characters. Another option has a simple but elegant solution that uses the fallen to represent an occasional byproduct of possession by demons from the Inferno. I would very much like to see a chapter like this in any future translation guides.</div> </div> </div> </div>This by far was my favorite part, and so far my favorite translation guide as well. Personally I think it explained and integrated both games best out of all of them. Quite a feat considering how disparate they seemed to each other as compared to the other template editions. Now hopefully after Mage Awakening comes out they could consider making a second edition version of the Translation guides in the same fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:41:56-07:00","id":567920,"title":"","content":"Actually, after reading the following passage on page 62, I wounder if the author saw my homebrew system (Demon the Possessed). I'd be so proud and grateful of notice if I'd somehow inspired someone at whitewolf. Even if not the case, I like the idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Reformed Possessors</b><br /> <i>&quot;I came into the world as a possessing spirit eager to corrupt it. I would bring a little bit of the Hell that was visited upon me by God to the Earth that He banished me from. But instead of becoming a second voice in my victim\u2019s mind, her consciousness joined with mine and her memories became my own. I\u2019m still a demon, an angel who defied God and spent eons in torment, but I\u2019m also her, also human. I can\u2019t tell you how great a gift that is.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The fallen angels are the demons of the Inferno. They are creatures of sin and abomination who corrupt and occasionally possess humans with the misfortune or poor judgment to invite them into the world. Occasionally, for reasons none of them understand, demon and host dissolve into each other to create one of the fallen. This tempers the madness of the demon and allows it to overcome its Torment enough to remember that it was once an angel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:48:48-07:00","id":567927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=567207#post567207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were Analysts intentionally not included in the guide? Because I could understand why, but it'd be nice to have an existing mechanical conversion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Book zero principle. With their word count, they really can't assume players will have anything than the other two cores.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:17:35-07:00","id":567976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=567927#post567927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book zero principle. With their word count, they really can't assume players will have anything than the other two cores.</div> </div> </div> </div>If one wanted to do Analysts, I'd say they'd probably favour Lore of Awakening, Lore of Humanity, Lore of Paths, Lore of Patterns, Lore of Portals, and Lore of Transfiguration. Off the top of my head. Otherwise you don't really need to convert anything else(?). Plus, the book just provides suggestions, rather than cost-break powers, and Embeds/Exploits are covered in chapter four.<br /> <br /> But yeah, this book is exactly what I wanted, and I've been awaiting it with bated breath since it was announced. Cheers to Eric for going through <i>every</i> form power, Background, and Merit from both the cores <i>and </i>the Players Guides and converting them. Having the <b>God-Machine</b> Merits converted to CWoD is super useful, and not just for <b>Demon</b> games.<br /> <br /> Cheers to Eric in general, really.<br /> <br /> Unless D20 (hee!) happens, I will probably never run <b>Fallen </b>with the old system again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 06-25-2015, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:25:53-07:00","id":567983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=567976#post567976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If one wanted to do Analysts, I'd say they'd probably favour Lore of Awakening, Lore of Humanity, Lore of Paths, Lore of Patterns, Lore of Portals, and Lore of Transfiguration. Off the top of my head. Otherwise you don't really need to convert anything else(?). Plus, the book just provides suggestions, rather than cost-break powers, and Embeds/Exploits are covered in chapter four.<br /> <br /> But yeah, this book is exactly what I wanted, and I've been awaiting it with bated breath since it was announced. Cheers to Eric for going through <i>every</i> form power, Background, and Merit from both the cores <i>and </i>the Players Guides and converting them. Having the <b>God-Machine</b> Merits converted to CWoD is super useful, and not just for <b>Demon</b> games.<br /> <br /> Cheers to Eric in general, really.<br /> <br /> Unless D20 (haha) happens, I will probably never run <b>Fallen </b>with the old system again.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know there IS a d20 wod fallen already ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (monte cooks world of darkness was it back then)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:53:38-07:00","id":568044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=567983#post567983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know there IS a d20 wod fallen already ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (monte cooks world of darkness was it back then)</div> </div> </div> </div>WE DON'T TALK ABOUT THAT.<br /> <br /> (I actually have a copy of MCWoD. The setting is total madness, and I kind of love that, but I'd never ever use it in a million years. Also I just don't like d20.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:24:32-07:00","id":568123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=566882#post566882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The best part was easily Hybrid Stories:</b> The final chapter provides something the past guides haven't: several setting alternatives for a cosmology that allows for the Fallen and the Unchained to coexist in a single world as two distinct types of fallen angel. There are some good ideas here, and the prose helps to break up the constant referring between books. A small majority of them lean towards folding the God-Machine into the Fallen cosmology as a sort of sub-phenomenon or deviation, but they generally do so pretty well, without damaging either perspective as characters. Another option has a simple but elegant solution that uses the fallen to represent an occasional byproduct of possession by demons from the Inferno. I would very much like to see a chapter like this in any future translation guides.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry it didn't quite have everything you were hoping for, but I'm glad you (and others) liked the hybrid stories. It's one of those things the other guides didn't have but I felt the Demons really needed. I heard a lot of people on forums wrestling with how to merge two games (as well as its oft-forgotten step-sister Inferno). As I was writing the Sebettu Conditions, it occurred to me that there is no reason why each Agenda should have just one possible Agenda Condition. I think you'd still want to limit it to just one per character, but it could reflect that demon's particular spin on the Agenda - some that provide one-use Social Merits based on the relationships demons with that Agenda tend to have, some that give the +3 bonus to certain situations, and so forth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=567927#post567927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book zero principle. With their word count, they really can't assume players will have anything than the other two cores.</div> </div> </div> </div>Book zero principle definitely came into play. I was kiiiinda pushing it by including the players guides, but that's the reason why Analysts and the Earthbound Lores (Chaos, Contamination, and Violation) didn't make it in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=566892#post566892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was kinda hoping for an actual, quick-ref translation for Descent's techno-terms into the more archaic flavoring of Fallen. You know, embed and exploits being called something more mystical, etc. Or at least having the option.</div> </div> </div> </div>It occurred to me to offer new names for each power (individual and broad category), but I didn't have the word count for it. Sorry to have disappointed you on that count.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=567976#post567976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, this book is exactly what I wanted, and I've been awaiting it with bated breath since it was announced. Cheers to Eric for going through <i>every</i> form power, Background, and Merit from both the cores <i>and </i>the Players Guides and converting them. Having the <b>God-Machine</b> Merits converted to CWoD is super useful, and not just for <b>Demon</b> games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad it lived up to your expectations. I know the wait dragged out longer than originally expected. Also, you caught me. I figured that since this was the first translation guide to translate a second edition game (even if we weren't quite calling it that at the time) it could also serve as a kind of translation between cWoD and nWoD2.0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:31:32-07:00","id":568128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=568123#post568123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I was writing the Sebettu Conditions, it occurred to me that there is no reason why each Agenda should have just one possible Agenda Condition. I think you'd still want to limit it to just one per character, but it could reflect that demon's particular spin on the Agenda - some that provide one-use Social Merits based on the relationships demons with that Agenda tend to have, some that give the +3 bonus to certain situations, and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a big part of the utility of the House Conditions to me, too; as a matter of fact, I'm already playing a Saboteur/Tempter with Multiple Agendas for whom I homebrewed a &quot;People Person&quot; Agenda Condition, because while living it up and enjoying existence in the human world are big elements of the character, showing up to parties and people's offices and jetsetting with the elite definitely aren't. (It asks a question of the Storyteller based on the character scoping out a person and gathering a read of her personality.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:36:04-07:00","id":568131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=568123#post568123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book zero principle definitely came into play. I was kiiiinda pushing it by including the players guides, but that's the reason why Analysts and the Earthbound Lores (Chaos, Contamination, and Violation) didn't make it in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just got my copy today, and I'm impressed with how much you did reference the player's guides. It's kinda ballsy.<br /> <br /> So, with getting that in there, I'm not surprised to see nothing beyond got in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:37:23-07:00","id":568132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=568123#post568123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm glad it lived up to your expectations. I know the wait dragged out longer than originally expected. Also, you caught me. I figured that since this was the first translation guide to translate a second edition game (even if we weren't quite calling it that at the time) it could also serve as a kind of translation between cWoD and nWoD2.0.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say it exceeded them! The mixed crossover stuff was just what I needed for a thing I can't talk about (because my players are on this forum). And I liked that you snuck in a more general translation. It's not something that any of the other Translation Guides were lacking, <i>per se</i>, but it really adds to the value of the book.<br /> <br /> And I don't think you pushed it too badly by including the Players Guides. In my experience, you <i>need </i>the Fallen Player's Guide to run that game at all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:40:49-07:00","id":568136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=568132#post568132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't think you pushed it too badly by including the Players Guides. In my experience, you <i>need </i>the Fallen Player's Guide to run that game at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I think the apocalyptic forms in the Player's Guide and the demonic forms in Descent parallel each other so closely as systems that not addressing the former would have been a major missed opportunity; it's one of the points in Descent where you really can see the design influence of Fallen, for the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:52:57-07:00","id":568143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=568136#post568136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I think the apocalyptic forms in the Player's Guide and the demonic forms in Descent parallel each other so closely as systems that not addressing the former would have been a major missed opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a big fan of Fallen, but the core mechanics are clunky, and it's full of weird mistakes and ambiguities. The DPG doesn't go all the way toward fixing that, but it seals up some of the cracks, and adds a lot that was missing. I'm keeping my fingers crossed for Demon20~2nd~4th~Revised~whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:55:34-07:00","id":568147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=568136#post568136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I think the apocalyptic forms in the Player's Guide and the demonic forms in Descent parallel each other so closely as systems that not addressing the former would have been a major missed opportunity; it's one of the points in Descent where you really can see the design influence of Fallen, for the better.</div> </div> </div> </div>True dat. Matt explicitly told me to plunder the Players Guide for the customizable form rules, and it was pretty self-evident why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T11:06:47-07:00","id":568194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=568147#post568147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True dat. Matt explicitly told me to plunder the Players Guide for the customizable form rules, and it was pretty self-evident why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eric Zawadzki! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T14:44:27-07:00","id":568399,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda bummed that the DTG didn't include anything of substance about the differences between DtF's \u201cThralldom pacting\u201d (in terms of what the Thrall gets out of the deal) and DtD's pacting rules, as they're very different from each other. But given how much there was to cover, it wasn't terribly surprising. <br /> <br /> BTW: shouldn't that \u201cthe Fallen are demons of the Inferno\u201d bit be in the Fallen-to-Descent section, as it's basically about how to incorporate the Fallen into the nWoD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T15:01:53-07:00","id":568413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=568399#post568399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW: shouldn't that \u201cthe Fallen are demons of the Inferno\u201d bit be in the Fallen-to-Descent section, as it's basically about how to incorporate the Fallen into the nWoD?</div> </div> </div> </div>I found the Hybrid Stories headers a bit misleading and confusing at first. &quot;The Fallen in Descent&quot; seems to denote settings that center on the Fallen as protagonists with the Unchained as a present X-factor, and &quot;The Unchained in Fallen&quot; the inverse. I didn't really think dividing up into those two sections was useful anyway, especially as there seemed to be a trend towards the primacy of the Fallen cosmology in both sections overall, with Reformed Possessors being the only setting of eight that really casts ambiguity on the origin of early Creation and the War of Wrath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T15:32:24-07:00","id":568438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=568399#post568399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda bummed that the DTG didn't include anything of substance about the differences between DtF's \u201cThralldom pacting\u201d (in terms of what the Thrall gets out of the deal) and DtD's pacting rules, as they're very different from each other. But given how much there was to cover, it wasn't terribly surprising.<br /> <br /> BTW: shouldn't that \u201cthe Fallen are demons of the Inferno\u201d bit be in the Fallen-to-Descent section, as it's basically about how to incorporate the Fallen into the nWoD?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I was hoping for a pact system to go with the Thrall merit. But, I made my own by combining both systems together, and making a few judgement calls. I, personally, like how mine turned out, but was hoping whatever one of the (better imo) writers could do with it. Oh well, I guess I'll get more use out of my system then. I think the DTG is great, and have been re-reading it.<br /> <br /> Also, is there a reason the Fallen don't add their perm. Faith to Evocation rules? The Unchained add their Primum to Exploits. I'd wager that it's the ability to spend Faith to buy dice, but I'm not sure if that makes up for it. <br /> <br /> Is it possible to use both Lores and Embed/Exploits as the Fallen? Or was it supposed to be one or the other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 06-25-2015, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T19:26:52-07:00","id":568669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=568413#post568413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I found the Hybrid Stories headers a bit misleading and confusing at first. &quot;The Fallen in Descent&quot; seems to denote settings that center on the Fallen as protagonists with the Unchained as a present X-factor, and &quot;The Unchained in Fallen&quot; the inverse. I didn't really think dividing up into those two sections was useful anyway, especially as there seemed to be a trend towards the primacy of the Fallen cosmology in both sections overall, with Reformed Possessors being the only setting of eight that really casts ambiguity on the origin of early Creation and the War of Wrath.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well to be fair it's kind of hard to do otherwise when one has people who remember the creation of the universe by an omniscient and omnipotent creator, and the other revolves around something that isn't omnipotent, omniscient, or universe creating as far as anyone knows.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T21:46:47-07:00","id":568762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=568438#post568438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I was hoping for a pact system to go with the Thrall merit. But, I made my own by combining both systems together, and making a few judgement calls. I, personally, like how mine turned out, but was hoping whatever one of the (better imo) writers could do with it. Oh well, I guess I'll get more use out of my system then. I think the DTG is great, and have been re-reading it.<br /> <br /> Also, is there a reason the Fallen don't add their perm. Faith to Evocation rules? The Unchained add their Primum to Exploits. I'd wager that it's the ability to spend Faith to buy dice, but I'm not sure if that makes up for it.<br /> <br /> Is it possible to use both Lores and Embed/Exploits as the Fallen? Or was it supposed to be one or the other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unchained don't add Primum to Embeds, but they add it to Exploits. I kind of had to choose one or the other and hope the bonus Faith dice helped the math meet the two kinds of powers in the middle. I also wanted to cleave more closely to the math of the root game when doing the conversion, and cWoD always felt a bit more failure-prone to me than nWoD does. If it feels weak in play to you and you want to make the characters more competent across the board, adding Faith to those rolls seems like a pretty easy solution to implement.<br /> <br /> You're completely welcome to mix-and-match the powers as long as your group is okay with it. I tried to get the power levels to mostly match, so the biggest problems I can see with mixing the two in the same characters are thematic - hellish/angelic Lores vs. spycraft/technological Embeds and Exploits. If you can reconcile those (I just plain didn't have the space, as mentioned earlier), you should be golden.<br /> <br /> As to a pact system, I'll admit it was one of the things that didn't occur to me at the time. I'm also a bit miffed that I didn't notice the lack of system in Fallen for locating new hosts until this thread. I probably didn't have enough space for either (much less both), but I still feel bad about those oversights. Sorry about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T22:12:38-07:00","id":568799,"title":"","content":"It's fine Eric. Space constraints are a major issue when there is just SO MUCH to do. So, I'm happy with what was included, because it was a tremendous help. <br /> <br /> As for Lores, my solution would be add Faith for the 3rd, 4th, and 5th dot of a Lore, since they corresponded to Exploits.As for Embeds, I'll probably go through and make a list of buyable ones, and make Torment effects for the Exploits (Evocations).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T22:27:33-07:00","id":568814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=568799#post568799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fine Eric. Space constraints are a major issue when there is just SO MUCH to do. So, I'm happy with what was included, because it was a tremendous help.<br /> <br /> As for Lores, my solution would be add Faith for the 3rd, 4th, and 5th dot of a Lore, since they corresponded to Exploits.As for Embeds, I'll probably go through and make a list of buyable ones, and make Torment effects for the Exploits (Evocations).</div> </div> </div> </div>Torment effects for Embeds/Exploits were another of those things that I wanted to include but just didn't have the space for. Maybe it's just because I spend so much time writing for these games, but I actually enjoy coming up with stuff like that. I had a glorious time putting a Descent spin on Fallen form powers, for example (solar powered demons!), and I'm a little ashamed at how much time I've spent designing house rules for my games. By which I mean that I hope that picking up where I had to leave off on high Torment Exploits will turn out to be more a source of fun for you than it is a chore. :-D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T00:34:05-07:00","id":568909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to a pact system, I'll admit it was one of the things that didn't occur to me at the time. I'm also a bit miffed that I didn't notice the lack of system in Fallen for locating new hosts until this thread. I probably didn't have enough space for either (much less both), but I still feel bad about those oversights. Sorry about that. </div> </div> </div>Nothing to be sorry about there. In essence it boils down to a normal possession rule anyway (at least how it was played in the groups I was in in fallen). Those that are &quot;broken&quot; enough are just easier to possess as their willpower is lower. And that is also what I'm going to use in descent there thus the normal possession rules and if you possess him......you have got a new host. <br /> That also makes possessing objects easier.....they got less willpower <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Btw the hybrid section even though it had no complete setting that rang a bell BUT it gave me quite a lot of ideas and a setting that rings a bell for me began to form.....currently putting it together to later on run it with a group <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> tnx for that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T06:07:00-07:00","id":569118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=568909#post568909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw the hybrid section even though it had no complete setting that rang a bell BUT it gave me quite a lot of ideas and a setting that rings a bell for me began to form.....currently putting it together to later on run it with a group <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> tnx for that!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're most welcome! :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T09:32:30-07:00","id":570304,"title":"","content":"For those interested, this is my homebrew rules for Possession and demons without a host.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>Dispossessed</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">When a demon's host is mortally wounded and they are unable to heal it, their spirit becomes untethered and manifests as their Apocalyptic Form above the body. The pain of death is only made worse by the Abyss, which they can feel pulling at them. They immediately lose one dot of Integrity, and gain a point of Torment as if they had failed a degeneration roll. While dispossessed, the Fallen has the traits of a ghost, with Power, Finesse, and Resistance attributes equal to the highest Attribute from their Power, Finesse or Resistance trait. Devils, Devourers, and Slayers have one higher Power, Fiends and Defilers have one higher Finesse, and Scourges and Malefactors have one higher Resistance. Regardless, they are unable to touch the material world and cannot use their Lores, but also cannot be affected by anything other than blessed items or powers specifically designed to affect spirits.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>Obtaining a New Host</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The demon cannot sustain themselves as pure spirits for long. Each minute they are without a host, the demon suffers a point of lethal damage. They may use what Aether they have to heal, but cannot ravage thralls or otherwise gain Aether. Once they take their Corpus in lethal or aggravated damage, the demon falls back into the Abyss. In order to avoid this fate, the demon must find a new suitable host\u2014one that is too spiritually weak or mentally dead to struggle\u2014and possess them quickly or fall back into the Abyss.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">A Finesse + Resistance roll can be made to sense a suitable host within a number of miles equal to their Exousia, with whatever penalty the ST feels is appropriate to find someone suitable in the area. If successful, the demon must travel towards them and attempt possession. Upon reaching a target, the demon can claim the body with a Power + Finesse roll; anyone who might conceivably be able to resist the possession attempt cannot be targeted by the demon. If they fail, they may try again, but at a cumulative -2 penalty. If the victim is a thrall that willingly accepts the possession, no roll is necessary.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Possessing a new body is a traumatic experience for the Fallen. Their memories and personality are once again melded with that of the host, often leading to crises of identity as priorities and beliefs shift. Pacts may break and even knowledge of Lores forgotten. The mortal world naturally rejects any connection between the Fallen's old persona and their new one, leading to the loss of Community and other Merits. ST and player are advised to stat the Fallen as a brand new character with the same amount of experience allocated to reflect the skill set and background of the new host, but keeping the demon's (modified) Exousia, Integrity, and Torment.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>Becoming Earthbound</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">If a suitable host cannot be found in time, the demon has one last shot: become one of the earthbound by binding their spirit to an object. No ordinary item will do, however; any would-be reliquary must resonant with humanity such that it could be considered unique or particularly special, and it must be discreet, not a part of some large object. The demon makes a Power + Finesse roll to attune the item to them, but they suffer a -3 penalty if it lacks mystical power or was not created to be a reliquary, and an additional -2 penalty if the object does not resonate with their House. Only one attempt may be made per object.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Once bound to an item, the Fallen is no longer pulled by the Abyss but also cannot leave their reliquary. They maintain the attributes they had as a dispossessed spirit and can manifest in their Apocalyptic Form by making a successful Power + Resistance roll, but they cannot move more than their Exousia in yards from their reliquary. Should the reliquary be destroyed the demon is freed, but they suffer the effects of having a host die and must once again seek sanctuary from the Abyss.<br /> ------------</span></span><br /> <br /> Exousia is what I call perm. Faith in my rules. Easy to substitute the names. Basically, they are ephermeral without any Manifestations or Numina. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T11:10:38-07:00","id":570344,"title":"","content":"And to Google I go...<br /> <br /> <b>exousia</b>--<i>n.</i> Greek. 1. power of choice, doing as one pleases. 2. physical and mental power. 3. the power of authority and of right.<br /> <br /> I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T18:07:22-07:00","id":570747,"title":"","content":"I am glad it is met with approval. xD I have more stuff in my signature if you are interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T18:05:21-07:00","id":572046,"title":"","content":"Okay I was trying to come up with new ways to mix fallen and the unchained, here's what I thought of:<br /> <br /> 1) The God-Machine is a quipolothic remnant of the previous universe.<br /> <br /> 2) The Fallen emerge from the Abyss, to find themselves in a new universe. No angels of the lord, a handful of Earthbound at most, a different afterlife, they find themselves strangers in a strange land....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T13:07:29-07:00","id":573068,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have a suggestions on how to turn the Inferno archetypes into either Agendas or Incarnations?<br /> <br /> For reference, the archetypes were<br /> <br /> Defiler<br /> Subversive<br /> Nemesis<br /> Slayer<br /> Tempter<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T15:43:55-07:00","id":573291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=573068#post573068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have a suggestions on how to turn the Inferno archetypes into either Agendas or Incarnations?<br /> <br /> For reference, the archetypes were<br /> <br /> Defiler<br /> Subversive<br /> Nemesis<br /> Slayer<br /> Tempter</div> </div> </div> </div>Defiler: Defilers are probably Saboteur Psychopomps, using their mastery of Infrastructure to &quot;defile&quot; bits of it for their own ends<br /> Subversive: Subversives are probably part of the Messenger Incarnation, but the Agenda they would follow is tough. Probably a double Agenda Inquisitor/Saboteur focusing on social Infrastructure<br /> Nemesis: Considering their roles as punishers, Destroyer seems appropriate, butI'm stumped as for Agenda. Complicated, methodical punishment may merit a Psychopomp.<br /> Slayer: Murder is their game, and Destroyers play it well. Again, Agenda's pretty uncertain here.<br /> Tempter: Well, the obvious choice here is the Tempter Agenda, probably coupled with the Messenger Incarnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T12:49:18-07:00","id":574233,"title":"","content":"Fair deal. Btw, does anyone know if MrGone'll make character sheets for this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T13:41:25-07:00","id":574327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=574233#post574233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair deal. Btw, does anyone know if MrGone'll make character sheets for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not unprompted, but he's pretty kind about filling requests if you ask him when he has the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T13:54:18-07:00","id":574331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=574327#post574327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably not unprompted, but he's pretty kind about filling requests if you ask him when he has the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mean, official character sheets for translation guide. Or is that the case?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T22:50:02-07:00","id":574808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=574331#post574331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I mean, official character sheets for translation guide. Or is that the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably nothing official (there are too many variables that people are picking and choosing from), but if you asked he'd very likely come up with one. He did for the Vampire Translation Guide, as I recall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T14:07:07-07:00","id":575602,"title":"","content":"Well shit, now I'm too shy to dare ask. ^_^;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T22:07:51-07:00","id":576031,"title":"","content":"Working on a side project thanks to this, listed below. Just so we are all clear, this is a sample of a work in progress:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Sans, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Demon Translation Guide Extra: Rituals</span></span><br /> Inspired from: <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies?cPath=8329_20642\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Sorcery Rites</a>, <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/123898/Vampire-The-Requiem-2nd-Edition?cPath=8329_20642\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire Devotions</a>, <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/57209/Hunter-The-Vigil?cPath=1_4561\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter Tactics</a>, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-creative-arts-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">Awakened Thaumaturgy Spell Factors</a>, <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/145541/Werewolf-the-Forsaken-2nd-Edition?cPath=8329_8592\" target=\"_blank\">Forsaken Rites</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/475-wyrd-sorcery\">Wyrd Sorcery</a><br /> A new Rite costs one half of an Experience point per dot, rounded up in the Ritual. Hadrisel's Libation, which requires Awakening 3 and Storms 1 costs 2 Experiences. (I've fiddled with the mix.)<br /> <b>Design Principles: </b>(Unless others stated, assume all costs listed in the Players Guide hold true)<ul><li>The Ankida: leader of the <b>teamwork action</b>, must know the Rite and the Primary Lore, selects target &amp; spell factors.</li> <li>The Mudu: supplemental actors, must have requisite knowledge of at least one of the Supplemental Lores and be willing to take direction from the Ankida.</li> <li>The Khauiki: Mostly redefined; tertiary actors, they act as power batteries (spending Faith/Willpower on behalf of Mudus who are running low) for the Rite and <i>reduce</i> <i>casting </i><i>penalties, </i>(rather than providing bonus dice). Still requires basic knowledge of one of the Lore Paths used in the Ritual. Think Yantras from M:tAw 2nd.</li> <li>Restrictions: By adding resonant limitations on the performance of the Rite (such as times, places, sacrifices, specialized equipment, etc), the power increases proportionally (measured by Spell Factors). This in addition to what the success are spent on, and never include Potency, (does include size, duration, distance, etc)</li> <li>The Sigil: (Yes, I'm still keeping it.) This includes all prep work, and at a minimum requires a (symbolically appropriate <i>physical</i>) circle with the Ankida &amp; Mudu evenly spread around. Any Khauiki must form a second circle outside that one.</li> <li>Casting Time: Limited by the lowest dicepool of all the Mudu, like all Extended Actions. Time interval between rolls is (Total Lore dots in Rite's Design multiplied Total Lore Paths in Rite) in minutes. eg; The revamped Hadrisel's Libation has each die roll every 8 minutes; needing 4 successes before the Ritual breaches threshold.</li> </ul><br /> *Includes Thralls, though they may have a smaller penalty if their knowledge of the Lores used exceeds the minimum.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The rules for Maintaining the Ritual (pg 184) function as normal (Stamina + Occult for Ankida &amp; Mudu), as do the rules for Losing Control (pg 184), Subverting Control &amp; Torment. Ignore the difficulties.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Faith Roll: Needs successes equal to Lore dots; extras spent on Spell Factors</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Mudu Dicepool: Attribute + Skill as appropriate based on non-prep Sigil</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 07-02-2015, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T18:02:20-07:00","id":578005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=574233#post574233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair deal. Btw, does anyone know if MrGone'll make character sheets for this?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=574327#post574327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not unprompted, but he's pretty kind about filling requests if you ask him when he has the time.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=574331#post574331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I mean, official character sheets for translation guide. Or is that the case?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=574808#post574808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably nothing official (there are too many variables that people are picking and choosing from), but if you asked he'd very likely come up with one. He did for the Vampire Translation Guide, as I recall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope I'm not too late.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> I haven't been asked to make Official Character Sheets for this. Guess OP gave up on trying to make character sheets for the translation guides. I did make some unofficial ones for the Vampire and Werewolf guides though(I wasn't being asked to make official sheets at the time those books came out).<br /> <br /> No ones asked me about doing these yet and I don't have the book. But, if someone wants to get me the info I'd need to make some new sheets, I'll see what I can do. Did they do any kind of cool hybrid border like they did for Vampire and Werewolf?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=575602#post575602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well shit, now I'm too shy to dare ask. ^_^;</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, don't be too shy. I never mind requests. I might not always get to them in as timely a manner as I'd like(I think I still have a few things in my requests folder from years ago), but I never mind people requesting things, so long as they don't mind if it's a bit of a wait. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T23:32:50-07:00","id":578315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=578005#post578005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hope I'm not too late.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I haven't been asked to make Official Character Sheets for this. Guess OP gave up on trying to make character sheets for the translation guides. I did make some unofficial ones for the Vampire and Werewolf guides though(I wasn't being asked to make official sheets at the time those books came out).<br /> <br /> No ones asked me about doing these yet and I don't have the book. But, if someone wants to get me the info I'd need to make some new sheets, I'll see what I can do. Did they do any kind of cool hybrid border like they did for Vampire and Werewolf?<br /> <br /> Nah, don't be too shy. I never mind requests. I might not always get to them in as timely a manner as I'd like(I think I still have a few things in my requests folder from years ago), but I never mind people requesting things, so long as they don't mind if it's a bit of a wait. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Please? Pretty please? I'd really like one, just one that ports over Torment, Lore and Faith (instead of Cover, Primiuim &amp; Aether).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T00:08:10-07:00","id":578354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=578005#post578005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No ones asked me about doing these yet and I don't have the book. But, if someone wants to get me the info I'd need to make some new sheets, I'll see what I can do. Did they do any kind of cool hybrid border like they did for Vampire and Werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>They did the hybrid layout again, yup. Here's a glance at a sample page for now.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/IumASZH\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/IumASZHm.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> As for info, there's various different possible combinations of traits, considering Torment and Cover could possibly coexist, Covers benefit from space for multiple but you only ever have one Torment rating, you could use Lores or Embeds and Exploits or even all three, etc. At least the demonic form/apocalyptic form is pretty similar in format. So it depends on what MrParaduo and FallenEco want, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T01:03:03-07:00","id":578382,"title":"","content":"So, why are Lores cheaper then Embeds or Exploits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T06:12:18-07:00","id":578656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=578382#post578382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, why are Lores cheaper then Embeds or Exploits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe because you can't use them in your Cipher. It'd make sense. The Earthbound distract you with the power and utility of Lores so that you don't unlock your true potential by internalizing embeds and exploits to rival their own power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T07:20:40-07:00","id":578727,"title":"","content":"Also, since high torment effects for embeds and exploits aren't a thing thanks to space restraints, lores are less reliable, or put into gadgets for giving them to your minions or making near or lambda gadgets based on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T08:21:20-07:00","id":578777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=578315#post578315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please? Pretty please? I'd really like one, just one that ports over Torment, Lore and Faith (instead of Cover, Primiuim &amp; Aether).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'll add it to my list. If you (or someone else) want to send me an email to better remind me, that'd be cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll see what I can do about the bit you're asking for....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=578354#post578354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They did the hybrid layout again, yup. Here's a glance at a sample page for now.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/IumASZH\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/IumASZHm.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't suppose you(or anyone else) can extract the border graphic for me, could you? If not, I can try to bug someone at OP and see if they can send it to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=578354#post578354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for info, there's various different possible combinations of traits, considering Torment and Cover could possibly coexist, Covers benefit from space for multiple but you only ever have one Torment rating, you could use Lores or Embeds and Exploits or even all three, etc. At least the demonic form/apocalyptic form is pretty similar in format. So it depends on what MrParaduo and FallenEco want, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like they made it a bit more complicated this time around. With Vampire and Werewolf it was basically just a port between the two systems, I don't remember there being options to port over separate system items. Of course, some of the systems in those games had the same name, so I guess it was easier for those.<br /> <br /> I guess it'll just be on a case by case basis then. I'm not sure I can make a sheet with all the different possible combos. Not even sure I can make a sheet with everything from both systems...hmmmm... Any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T08:30:03-07:00","id":578795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=578777#post578777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it'll just be on a case by case basis then. I'm not sure I can make a sheet with all the different possible combos. Not even sure I can make a sheet with everything from both systems...hmmmm... Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Make them detachable sections? Like put a toggle switch somewhere on the interactive page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T12:55:10-07:00","id":579085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=578795#post578795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make them detachable sections? Like put a toggle switch somewhere on the interactive page.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've briefly played around with the idea of layers, when it comes to borders and such. It'd be much harder to do different sections of a sheet, especially since it'd be hard to figure out how to make all the different combos fit together properly...<br /> <br /> Not a bad idea though, might be worth looking into to...not sure I can pull it off, but I can always try. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T12:56:59-07:00","id":579087,"title":"","content":"I believe in you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: What if Torment replaced Primum? It'd represent your attempt at balancing the human soul with the temptations of Hell. It'd almost work like an inverted Humanity trait from VtR, in that the higher it gets, the more demonic you appear (glitches, fiendish flaws, and the like).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 07-04-2015, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T09:46:08-07:00","id":583548,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea: what if <i>both</i> sides had infrastructure? Only the Angels're more unified, but the Demons are harder to destroy outright due to diverse agencies, alliances, and individual stratagems?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T11:44:48-07:00","id":583687,"title":"","content":"That raises another idea: should we design a system of for developing demonic infrastructure? Maybe something like the Zero-sum mechanic that's used when designing Pacts. Eg, the trickier it is is to build, the lower the cost gets, while the more beneficial it is, as well as how easy to detect and/or guard, raises the cost. And maybe that's just for the <i>blueprint.</i> You still need to get everything into place, which could be a whole chronicle in and of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T21:28:42-07:00","id":586764,"title":"","content":"So. Yay. New book. And I'm always all over new demon stuff. So. How much of this if any can I use if I don't have demon the fallen. Like is the translation guide 100% useless without having both cores?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T21:40:42-07:00","id":586771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=586764#post586764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Yay. New book. And I'm always all over new demon stuff. So. How much of this if any can I use if I don't have demon the fallen. Like is the translation guide 100% useless without having both cores?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say about 66% useless - If you've got just DtD you can use the stuff that's about converting into OWoD mechanics, plus there's the mixed chronicle stuff with guidelines on having stories and cosmology involving both the Fallen and the Unchained.<br /> <br /> But it's definitely something you want both cores to appreciate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T21:52:02-07:00","id":586775,"title":"","content":"Aw pity. I was hoping the lord and form aborted would have been reprinted with 2nd Ed rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T22:21:25-07:00","id":586810,"title":"","content":"It does give mechanics from converting stuff from the Core and the uh, Player's Guide? (Or was it the ST's guide?). But the stuff is pretty dense - it's crammed into ~70 pages all up. There's very brief summaries of all the incarnations and houses and whatnot, but they've clearly decided to be as efficient as they can with words.<br /> <br /> I'm not personally super familiar with Fallen, but I've been reading my partner's copy because reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T22:41:03-07:00","id":586818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=586764#post586764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Yay. New book. And I'm always all over new demon stuff. So. How much of this if any can I use if I don't have demon the fallen. Like is the translation guide 100% useless without having both cores?</div> </div> </div> </div>Notable mechanical widgets that don't at all require Demon: the Fallen to reference or grok:<ul><li><b>House Conditions:</b> A new Agenda Condition for each of the seven Houses of the Fallen, pretty easily adaptable as custom Agenda Conditions for Descent characters: Stormy Temper, Self-Doubt, Straight Talk, Curiosity, Better with Tools, Cynical and Outsider's View.</li> <li><b>Converted Merits:</b> Certain Merits from DtF are converted as nWoD Merits, and twelve of these do not reference the original text and do not require conditions native to Fallen and not Descent: Angelic Aura, Angelic Gaze, Atavistic Form, Acute Sense, Forgettable, Good Night Vision, Daredevil, Enchanting Voice, Lucky, Code of Honor, Fast Learner and Eye for a Bargain.</li> <li><b>Demonic Form Abilities:</b> The apocalyptic form powers are either directed to preexisting analogues in Descent or converted as new demonic form abilities (sometimes both). Nearly all of the converted form abilities provide the full rules to use in Descent, including a sample appearance in Descent's biomechanical aesthetic, and most of the ones that reference the text of Fallen have names that kind of tell you what you need to know anyway (Casts No Reflection and Immune to Poison, for example). There are 11 new Modifications, 15 new Technologies and 11 new Processes. (No new Propulsions.)</li> <li><b>Hybrid Stories:</b> The final chapter is pure fluff and could be interesting reading for gathering Descent inspiration even if you're not specifically planning to cross over with Fallen.</li> </ul><br /> Lores are a little more involved. Lores are structured in 1-5 dot scales like vampiric Disciplines, with a new evocation at every dot of the Lore, but not every lore provides converted rules for all five of its evocations; lores that can just port over dice pools and effects fairly straight are omitted and just reference a chart for adjusting difficulties. For the most part, I would say that I would really want to have the DtF book to reference when reading over even the lores with detailed converted rules. There are some evocations that run so long that they might function on their own, but they're not the rule; if nothing else, most lack useful context.<br /> <br /> But for that many usable demonic form abilities in that little space, for that small a price? I'd go for it. My character in my weekly Descent game happened to recently raise Primum, so I've already swapped in Casts No Reflection and Relentless for a swank mechanical stealth form, in addition to a homebrew power that isn't Eyes of Fate, but which was inspired by reading Eyes of Fate.<br /> <br /> \u2014 aaand shit, in the process of tallying these up for you I noticed a significant erratum after the errata thread's already closed. The apocalyptic form power Immune to Falling Damage says to substitute Abruption Jets or just use as written in Fallen, but doesn't specify what form ability the &quot;use as written&quot; form falls under. I infer it would probably be a Modification from the trend with similar powers, but it's a significant omission.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit:</i> Removed Good Recognition from the usable Merits list. For running one of the Fallen in the Storytelling System it's fine, if a bit niche, but it's mostly irrelevant to the Unchained, who already exhibit devilish memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 07-11-2015, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T22:47:36-07:00","id":586823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=586818#post586818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2014 aaand shit, in the process of tallying these up for you I noticed a significant erratum after the errata thread's already closed. The apocalyptic form power Immune to Falling Damage says to substitute Abruption Jets or just use as written in Fallen, but doesn't specify what form ability the &quot;use as written&quot; form falls under. I infer it would probably be a Modification from the trend with similar powers, but it's a significant omission.</div> </div> </div> </div>Send off a Private Message to Eric, you might just sneak in before it's too late and it is immortalised in print forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T23:02:10-07:00","id":586829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcod