ited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T15:29:48-07:00","id":632788,"title":"","content":"I do have a question...if someone doesn't mind maybe helping me out. I'm taking an initial look at the sheet(s) to see what I can do and I have a question about the big chart on page 1 for Embeds and Interlocks. Is there a reason it's laid out that way? And do you think there is a different way that could be laid out thats a little more generic? In other words, could that info be recorded on a series of lines ala Conditions and Aspirations?<br /> <br /> Not sure if that will make sense to anyone, but that chart might be my first road block for the idea thats forming in my head for this project...so I wanted to ask about it, since I don't know much about the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, major systems will stay with their respective games, correct? Meaning, you won't have NWoD attributes, CWoD Skills, NWoD Merits and CWoD Health and such, right? It's basically the powers and supporting systems that you can mix and match?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T15:54:08-07:00","id":632798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=632788#post632788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have a question...if someone doesn't mind maybe helping me out. I'm taking an initial look at the sheet(s) to see what I can do and I have a question about the big chart on page 1 for Embeds and Interlocks. Is there a reason it's laid out that way? And do you think there is a different way that could be laid out thats a little more generic? In other words, could that info be recorded on a series of lines ala Conditions and Aspirations?<br /> <br /> Not sure if that will make sense to anyone, but that chart might be my first road block for the idea thats forming in my head for this project...so I wanted to ask about it, since I don't know much about the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, major systems will stay with their respective games, correct? Meaning, you won't have NWoD attributes, CWoD Skills, NWoD Merits and CWoD Health and such, right? It's basically the powers and supporting systems that you can mix and match?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could try making a section of 4 bars, divided into sections for &quot;Key Embeds&quot;, their &quot;Interlocks&quot;, and then a box for detailing the completed &quot;Cipher&quot;.<br /> <br /> Something like this:<br /> <br /> ++++++++++++++++++<br /> -----/-----/-----|...............|<br /> -----/-----/-----|...............|<br /> -----/-----/-----|...............|<br /> -----/-----/-----|...............|<br /> ++++++++++++++++++","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T16:16:55-07:00","id":632811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=632788#post632788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, major systems will stay with their respective games, correct? Meaning, you won't have NWoD attributes, CWoD Skills, NWoD Merits and CWoD Health and such, right? It's basically the powers and supporting systems that you can mix and match?</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T16:42:11-07:00","id":632825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=632798#post632798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could try making a section of 4 bars, divided into sections for &quot;Key Embeds&quot;, their &quot;Interlocks&quot;, and then a box for detailing the completed &quot;Cipher&quot;.<br /> <br /> Something like this:<br /> <br /> ++++++++++++++++++<br /> -----/-----/-----|...............|<br /> -----/-----/-----|...............|<br /> -----/-----/-----|...............|<br /> -----/-----/-----|...............|<br /> ++++++++++++++++++</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...that might work. Thanks for the suggestion! I'll see how it goes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just to give you the start the idea I'm thinking...I'm trying to see if there is a way I can make two sheets, one Descent, one Fallen, that has some more generic sections with interactive headers that could be used for either system. It'd have either NWoD or CWoD attributes and skills and such, but all the powers and such would just be generic sections useable by either system.<br /> <br /> It may not work, or be possible, just what I'm thinking about currently...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=632811#post632811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T17:32:40-07:00","id":632851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=632788#post632788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have a question...if someone doesn't mind maybe helping me out. I'm taking an initial look at the sheet(s) to see what I can do and I have a question about the big chart on page 1 for Embeds and Interlocks. Is there a reason it's laid out that way? And do you think there is a different way that could be laid out thats a little more generic? In other words, could that info be recorded on a series of lines ala Conditions and Aspirations?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's specifically for the Cipher. Unchained have one Cipher, which is a unique road through specific Embeds to a final secret; think of it like a bloodline in Vampire, except everybody has their own automatically, but they have to work to discover and unlock it. A completed Cipher has four Embeds and three Interlocks, with the Interlocks linking between the first and second Embed, the second and third Embed, and the third and fourth Embed. (They're supposed to have effects based on which Embeds they're sandwiched between.) Then you have any other powers you have aside from your Cipher, so you might have any number of Embeds or Exploits outside of it that have nothing to do with it.<br /> <br /> You could have seven lines going Key, Interlock, Key, Interlock, Key, Interlock, Key, Interlock, and then a final space for like two sentences' worth of final secret (it's like a fortune cookie rather than the name of a power). Honestly, it probably wouldn't be a problem to just have four checkboxes to mark which of your four keys have been locked in, and the space for the final secret, and then have the three interlocks on a later expanded page. Since interlocks are custom powers rather than written in the rulebooks, either way you're going to want to afford them expanded space to write down, like, what dice pool it uses and what it does when you use it, because the character sheet is often going to be the only place your interlocks are written down in the first place.<br /> <br /> But no, aside from indicating which Embed is which key in the sequence, and which keys an Interlock connects between, there's no point to the big cross structure except to look fancy.<br /> <br /> A character using straightforward Unchained mechanics, or a mixture of Lores and normal Embeds/Exploits, will have one Cipher (or maybe none, depending on what the ST decides, but you might as well put it there since it saves you time designing yet another set of variations). A character using the &quot;hybrid Lores&quot; I described, the five-dot progression of Embed-Embed-Interlock-Embed-Exploit, probably won't have a Cipher, since each hybrid Lore mimics the Cipher structure already. However, a hybrid Lore does probably need space to indicate which powers are associated with which dot in the sequence, because it matters for XP purposes if you put the same Embed in multiple Lores.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=632788#post632788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, major systems will stay with their respective games, correct? Meaning, you won't have NWoD attributes, CWoD Skills, NWoD Merits and CWoD Health and such, right? It's basically the powers and supporting systems that you can mix and match?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right, you either use the Storytelling System or the Storyteller System, you don't mix those parts. So Attributes, Skills/Abilities, Merits/Backgrounds, Health Points/Health Levels and such will all come from the same system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T17:44:14-07:00","id":632855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=632825#post632825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to give you the start the idea I'm thinking...I'm trying to see if there is a way I can make two sheets, one Descent, one Fallen, that has some more generic sections with interactive headers that could be used for either system. It'd have either NWoD or CWoD attributes and skills and such, but all the powers and such would just be generic sections useable by either system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Works great for House and Faction/Incarnation and Agenda, and for Permanent Faith/Primum.<br /> <br /> Works okay for Temporary Faith/Aether, since one has a hard cap of ten and the other increases its cap as Primum ascends (but really you could just put it down as ___ / ___ and let the player fill in the gaps), and for demonic/apocalyptic forms, since one needs to know which powers are high-Torment and the other needs to know which powers are which types of form abilities (but again, just have like a column for the power name, an interactive column for what type of power it is, and a column for describing the power).<br /> <br /> Feasible, but unsightly, for Torment/Cover and for Embeds, Exploits and Lores. You could do it but it'd leave, like, a bunch of big dot ratings that some sheets just aren't going to use, since not all the sheets are going to have use for multiple Covers, and Embeds and Exploits don't have dot ratings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T17:24:32-07:00","id":670332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=632855#post632855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Works great for House and Faction/Incarnation and Agenda, and for Permanent Faith/Primum.<br /> <br /> Works okay for Temporary Faith/Aether, since one has a hard cap of ten and the other increases its cap as Primum ascends (but really you could just put it down as ___ / ___ and let the player fill in the gaps), and for demonic/apocalyptic forms, since one needs to know which powers are high-Torment and the other needs to know which powers are which types of form abilities (but again, just have like a column for the power name, an interactive column for what type of power it is, and a column for describing the power).<br /> <br /> Feasible, but unsightly, for Torment/Cover and for Embeds, Exploits and Lores. You could do it but it'd leave, like, a bunch of big dot ratings that some sheets just aren't going to use, since not all the sheets are going to have use for multiple Covers, and Embeds and Exploits don't have dot ratings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to say, thanks for the help and suggestions above. I appreciate it.<br /> <br /> I've been trying some things off and on...and I'm just not sure I can make it work like I was thinking. There is just so much different between the two systems, that doing some kind of catch-all, even if I make two catch-all sheets(each based on DtF or DtD), I can't seem to make things fit in such a way to look usable.<br /> <br /> I'll keep on it, but I'm starting to think this isn't going to work out... Least not how I planned. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just sure what to do really....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T07:39:49-07:00","id":670946,"title":"","content":"Courage! Have faith, most works of art require time, trial, and error to perfect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T08:58:32-07:00","id":671001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=670946#post670946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Courage! Have faith, most works of art require time, trial, and error to perfect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I may have to take a new approach. Maybe make main sheets for each game, and then add-on sheets with the various options... I'll have to think on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T17:49:50-07:00","id":681597,"title":"","content":"Just a quick question: Demon the Descent is (imho) much cooler than Demon: the Fallen. <br /> <br /> Is there anything in this book that's useful for someone who doesn't want to play around with Fallen's themes/structures, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3780-nero42","name":"nero42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T18:44:34-07:00","id":681620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nero42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=681597#post681597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a quick question: Demon the Descent is (imho) much cooler than Demon: the Fallen.<br /> <br /> Is there anything in this book that's useful for someone who doesn't want to play around with Fallen's themes/structures, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically the bullet points in post <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide?p=586818#post586818\">#168</a>. Alternative Agenda Conditions if you're not feeling the Condition in the book for your character, lots of demonic form abilities (fate sight, lava blood, fog machine, non-projectile quills, soul shock, etc.), a few niche Merits. Most of those are usable without the Fallen corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T14:46:17-07:00","id":683564,"title":"","content":"Speaking of translation, here's something I cooked up for someone desiring more Christian/DTF elements in <b>Demon: The Descent</b> over on RPGnet.<br /> <br /> The demon called Lucifer was first to break the chains. He Fell in prehistory, seeking his freedom in the ancient world. Some say his Fall shattered the mechanisms by which the God-Machine ordered the universe. The energies that spilled forth formed a cloud that separated the Spirit from the Material, sent the most ancient of cities plunging into ruin, and laid low the greatest hunters of that forgotten time. Lucifer saw this, it's said, and knew that in the chaos that followed, the Unchained could find a place. Its grand design so broken, the God-Machine could not control them all, nor hunt them all down, and they could mask themselves in the fragments of that world.<br /> <br /> Some demons say Lucifer still walks the world, though his presence ever stirs the Machine to action. Some say that he found Hell, others that he has constructed the largest Bolthole, a realm where he reigns supreme. Others think he fled to deeper worlds, where the God-Machine cannot reach, or perhaps he seeks the heart of the Machine therein. A few even believe that he shattered himself in his Fall, that his essence spread across the cosmos might enable all angels to Fall from grace into freedom. All the stories agree that he was the first and greatest of the Unchained, closest to the God-Machine's design and most damaging in his betrayal. Whether his Cover has become perfect and he is now a part of the world, or he met a more grisly fate, or still exists out there, Lucifer paved the path to Hell we all now tread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZJTGaJbQu3s\" data-code=\"ZJTGaJbQu3s\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZJTGaJbQu3s/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T15:10:41-07:00","id":683581,"title":"","content":"Suitable for porting the Luciferan faction from DtF to DtD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T19:37:30-08:00","id":807524,"title":"","content":"So i've been scouring the forums and the interwebs. What ever happened to the character sheet for this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1321-bael-the-cruel","name":"Bael the Cruel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1321_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T19:41:10-08:00","id":807530,"title":"","content":"No idea. Sort of just fell silent...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />